## Run locally

```sh
{% for wl in repo.workloads %}
(cd {{ wl.source_dir or "." }} && python -m app.main)   # {{ wl.name }}{% if wl.port %}, http://localhost:{{ wl.port }}{{ defaults.HEALTH_PATH }}{% endif %}

{% endfor %}
```

Tests use the standard library:

```sh
{% for wl in repo.workloads %}
(cd {{ wl.source_dir or "." }} && python -m unittest discover -s tests -t .)
{% endfor %}
```

## CI with Dagger

The pipeline lives in `.dagger/` and runs the same way locally and in CI
(needs [Dagger](https://docs.dagger.io) {{ defaults.DAGGER_VERSION }} and Docker):

```sh
dagger call workloads           # list discovered workloads
dagger call test                # run every workload's tests
dagger call build --workload=NAME
dagger call ship --commit=$(git rev-parse HEAD) \
  --registry-username=USER --registry-password=env://REGISTRY_PASSWORD \
  --git-token=env://GITOPS_TOKEN
```

`ship` tests, pushes `{{ project.registry }}/{{ project.name }}-<workload>:<commit>` for each workload,
then commits `environments/{{ defaults.RELEASE_ENVIRONMENT }}/<workload>/release.yaml` to
[{{ plan.gitops.folder }}]({{ plan.gitops.url }}). Argo CD deploys from there.

{% if project.git_provider.value == "github" %}
`.github/workflows/ci.yaml` runs `test` on pull requests and `ship` on pushes to `main`. Set these
repository secrets:

- `GITOPS_TOKEN`: a token that can push to `{{ plan.gitops.folder }}`
- `REGISTRY_PASSWORD`: only if the registry is not `ghcr.io` (otherwise `GITHUB_TOKEN` is used)

and, for registries other than `ghcr.io`, the repository variable `REGISTRY_USERNAME`.
{% elif project.git_provider.value == "gitlab" %}
`.gitlab-ci.yml` runs `test` on merge requests and `ship` on pushes to the default branch. Set these
CI/CD variables (masked): `GITOPS_TOKEN`, `REGISTRY_USERNAME`, `REGISTRY_PASSWORD`.
{% else %}
No CI provider file was generated. Run the `dagger call` commands above from your CI system.
{% endif %}
